# the C fragment ratchet (tests/run.sh): the GNU forms s2c --fragment lists but does not fail, summed per kind over the El
# constructors. a cell that GROWS fails the gate; a cell that SHRINKS fails it too, until this file is updated in the same
# change (the base only goes down; s2c rows only report). rows: <input> <kind> <count>. corpus = bench/corpus (corpus-self input), s2c = the
# current s2c source (it moves with every s2 edit: update the s2c rows with it), tiny = tests/s2/fragbase/tiny.srs (armed:
# tests/s2/fragbase/tiny_grow.srs has one extra match and must fail against these rows)
corpus address-of 1
corpus auto-type 12698
corpus goto-out 1134
corpus stmt-expr 14850
s2c address-of 2
s2c auto-type 22446
s2c goto-out 2071
s2c stmt-expr 26153
tiny address-of 0
tiny auto-type 39
tiny goto-out 4
tiny stmt-expr 73
